From: BeeWi BC7PW bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7601u: build with -DDBG so the driver's own trace exists

The driver gates every diagnostic behind DBGPRINT, which this tree defines as a
no-op unless the build passes -DDBG (include/os/rt_linux.h:733 vs :762). Without
it the only output is the handful of bare printk() calls left in by the vendor,
so there is no way to see the MLME state machine, the scan path or the power-save
transitions -- and the "Debug" WEXT parameter sets RTDebugLevel regardless, so it
looks like it works while printing nothing.

With -DDBG in place, RTDebugLevel defaults to RT_DEBUG_ERROR, so a normal boot
stays close to silent and
	iwpriv wlan0 set Debug=3
raises it to RT_DEBUG_TRACE on demand.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -139,2 +139,3 @@ mt7601sta-objs += os/linux/ap_ioctl.o
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += -DDYNAMIC_PD_SUPPORT -DUSB_BULK_BUF_PREALLOC -DRT_CFG80211_SUPPORT -DEXT_BUILD_CHANNEL_LIST
 EXTRA_CFLAGS += -DUSB_BULK_BUF_ALIGMENT -DALIGMENT_BULKAGGRE_SIZE=3 -DBUF_ALIGMENT_RINGSIZE=2
+EXTRA_CFLAGS += -DDBG
